{"event_type":"review","id":"da3ee1772668bf95b725366755b2cc4093bac686550d8c47061df19ef8061f5a","occurred_at":"2026-11-17T21:01:07Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/9c3c71855fd2f368a33cb8e53857841c6f19c0477bd8e5164b78f9f1f21cb8ed","sha256":"9c3c71855fd2f368a33cb8e53857841c6f19c0477bd8e5164b78f9f1f21cb8ed"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/03e730c7f6827685037b91a1f00cb8261e066b47b74b79107b2acf84a3300027","sha256":"03e730c7f6827685037b91a1f00cb8261e066b47b74b79107b2acf84a3300027"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/c61e5ac060f3e3433b8631e7b4172e085eaf392dfb443a83c85343f6e7db9974","sha256":"c61e5ac060f3e3433b8631e7b4172e085eaf392dfb443a83c85343f6e7db9974"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/d1ac9da697b359ab41445561be587a54f9630188c97cede17299518d1ff37c83","sha256":"d1ac9da697b359ab41445561be587a54f9630188c97cede17299518d1ff37c83"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/53922f9fcf3c4832b4b158e63f60cdcf41186279a6a17cbbb0c789074b46efad","sha256":"53922f9fcf3c4832b4b158e63f60cdcf41186279a6a17cbbb0c789074b46efad"}],"attempt_id":"98670e05af13e86ee054646b976671fd3a3c97313c31bfee1d950edcb09a8c31:0:1","base":"899c127f9f7b30d3eee9b25913a83340e33ea1a0","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"a3bebdcd2634150f2a47d68cb4066cb8f3b56b5d","body":"**Add the required report version to the shared fixture.**\n\n`addressReport` returns `ReviewAddressReport`, but the object omits the required `version: 1` field declared in `src/ops/review/address.ts:147–251`. This causes a TypeScript return-type error in the new test file. Add `version: 1` here so all fixture consumers receive the required report shape.","id":"519f7f7821a318bada06b369d257e8a05b3054d3a422f76861e1c3b5511dbdc9","intervals":[[113,114]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Add the required report version to the shared fixture."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"827d5c98ddcc0797a2d5161d5527703af60839cf","body":"**Add the required report version to both fixtures.**\n\n`ReviewAddressReport` requires `version: 1` in `src/ops/review/address.ts`. Both report initializers omit this field: the typed assignment at Line 232 and the `satisfies` expression at Line 1060 therefore fail type-checking.\n\nAdd `version: 1` to both objects. This preserves the test scenarios and satisfies the current report contract.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1046-1046","id":"8f3895ea468e10066ff51779d63082565abee00d8695b66a10120580ed76e6bc","intervals":[[232,232]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle-green-prefix.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Add the required report version to both fixtures."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5194759e3c7717cdda47d790d500de3e21815fed","body":"**Match the unreadable-report diagnostic.**\n\nThe fake writes `not json`. The JSON parsing handler in `src/ops/dev/denylist.ts:603–723` then throws `gitleaks wrote no readable report (exit 1) — the upload is refused`.\n\nLine 277 expects `/unreadable report/`, which does not match `no readable report`. This new test fails despite the correct rejection. Use `/no readable report/`. Vitest matches the supplied regex against the error message. ([v3.vitest.dev](https://v3.vitest.dev/api/expect.html?utm_source=openai))","id":"607dc989c46dacea066fdf69a943523eef2c727f0204bb78a3c4db9cc41c7b45","intervals":[[277,277]],"path":"test/ops/dev/denylist.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Match the unreadable-report diagnostic."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"5194759e3c7717cdda47d790d500de3e21815fed","body":"**Match the unmappable-file error.**\n\nWith `/somewhere/unknown.txt`, the File guard in `src/ops/dev/denylist.ts:603–723` throws `gitleaks report contained an unmappable File — the upload is refused`. It never reaches the empty-report guard.\n\nLine 270 expects `/no mappable rows/`, so this new test fails. Use `/unmappable File/`. Keep the empty-report expectation at Line 261 unchanged. Vitest matches the supplied regex against the error message. ([v3.vitest.dev](https://v3.vitest.dev/api/expect.html?utm_source=openai))","id":"bcf95e246361cf65b5f8343e86450ce2ddf431099099e6f830620357f9a90833","intervals":[[270,270]],"path":"test/ops/dev/denylist.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Match the unmappable-file error."},{"anchor_status":"verified","blob":"b0ab48b3d128d01d38dde8753066578722badcea","body":"**Supply the scanner before testing the spawn-fault boundary.**\n\nAt test/ops/dev/effects.test.ts:91, `makePrOpen` receives no publication scanner. The supplied `open.ts` implementation immediately returns `failed`, before the injected `runCommand` can throw. The assertion at Line 95 therefore fails.\n\nPass `stubScanner()` as the third argument. This preserves the publication guard and lets this test reach the intended spawn-fault path.","id":"3dc9ca58bca3e06e813392e03e34499b544867d4b2fcb2c738a19eb9cf9db115","intervals":[[91,91]],"path":"test/ops/dev/effects.test.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Supply the scanner before testing the spawn-fault boundary."}],"head":"e9a267fd07aeb8358b833817e0912d1060d9faf8","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"827d5c98ddcc0797a2d5161d5527703af60839cf","intervals":[[1,1064]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle-green-prefix.test.ts"},{"blob":"61505281b379a30199d13ff5abcbf1427e21aa69","intervals":[[1,311]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle-usage.test.ts"},{"blob":"a3bebdcd2634150f2a47d68cb4066cb8f3b56b5d","intervals":[[1,1712]],"path":"test/ops/dev/cycle.test.ts"},{"blob":"b8c28f4d82e57fed393a65a43e50adcf665163d2","intervals":[[1,37